  "summary_en": "European Parliamentary Research Service briefing (fourth edition, September 2024) tracing the EU AI Act from the 2021 Commission proposal to adoption as Regulation (EU) 2024/1689. It explains the risk-based tiers, prohibited practices, high-risk obligations, GPAI rules, scope, and governance, with only incidental product-safety references to embodied systems.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "AI Act is the first binding horizontal AI regulation, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, published 12 July 2024.",
   "Four-tier risk approach: prohibited, high-risk, limited-risk transparency, minimal risk.",
   "High-risk systems include safety components of products such as toys, cars, medical devices and lifts, with conformity assessment.",
   "Special rules for GPAI models, with stricter duties for systemic-risk models.",
   "Military, defence, national security and pure research uses are excluded from scope."
